amine in mild cognitive impairment studies</article-title><source>Aust Adv Drug Reactions Bull</source><volume>25</volume><issue>1</issue><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.tga.gov.au/adr/aadrb/aadr0602.htm&#x00023;a1">http://www.tga.gov.au/adr/aadrb/aadr0602.htm&#x00023;a1</ext-link>. Accessed 31 October 2007.</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040338-b043"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Carli</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Frisoni</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Harvey</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Grundman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Qualitative estimates of medial temporal atrophy as a predictor of progression from mild cognitive impairment to dementia</article-title><source>Arch Neurol</source><volume>64</volume><fpage>108</fpage><lpage>115</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17210817</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040338-b044"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frisoni</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Canu</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Geroldi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Zanetti</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Zacchi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Drug prescription in mild cognitive impairment: the physicians' perspective in Italy</article-title><source>Int J Geriatr Psychiatry</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>1071</fpage><lpage>1077</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16955446</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040338-b045"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name